  "title": "Vectors",
  "content": "<p>A <strong>vector</strong> has magnitude and direction. Written as \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) or \\(\\binom{x}{y}\\). The negative reverses direction: \\(-\\mathbf{a}\\) or \\(\\binom{-x}{-y}\\).</p><p><strong>Route finding:</strong> To get from A to B, use any route through known vectors: \\(\\overrightarrow{AB} = \\overrightarrow{AO} + \\overrightarrow{OB} = -\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b}\\).</p><p><strong>Midpoints:</strong> If M is the midpoint of AB, then \\(\\overrightarrow{AM} = \\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{AB}\\). <strong>Parallel vectors:</strong> If \\(\\overrightarrow{PQ} = k\\overrightarrow{RS}\\), the lines are parallel.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>OA = a, OB = b. Find AB.</strong></p><p>\\(\\overrightarrow{AB} = \\overrightarrow{AO} + \\overrightarrow{OB} = -\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a}\\)</p>"
 },
